## Tiering Model
- `mcp`: use for tool discovery, agent execution, platform configuration, schema introspection, Living Memory recall/store. Avoid chatty runtime CRUD loops, high-frequency telemetry polling, bulk app-owned data sync.
- `public_rest`: use for browser/runtime access to governed Memory, IoT, DAM, Entity, PIM, Relationships, Agents, and domain Events. Avoid database administration, returning raw credentials, bypassing API Expose bindings.
- `direct_mongo`: use for PLATFORM-INTERNAL ONLY. Not available to application code. App data access goes through DC agents with mongodb MCP steps called via /public/agents/execute.. Avoid Everything. Application code MUST NEVER use MongoClient, mongoose, or any direct MongoDB driver..
- `pulsar`: use for platform-internal event-driven ingestion, telemetry fan-out, interpreter normalization, async workflows. Avoid direct browser consumption, direct app-instance writes (use platform API endpoints instead).

## App Architecture Guide
- Summary: How to build apps on DevCockpit. Read this before creating agents or inserting data.
- Data rule: The frontend is never source of truth. All app data goes through the contextualizer / governed doors into the seat's own database (PIM, Entity Registry, Living Memory, DAM, Relationships) — that is why each app has a database. SPA JSON, localStorage, sessionStorage, baked public/data, and committed zip media are cache only after a store-read proves persisted ids.
- PIM: Use the PIM-cluster structure store (dc__pim_upsert) for templates routeToPlane() sends to pim (built_artifacts, assets, catalog products). Products, compatibility, and catalog rows live in PIM — first write is propose→confirm→upsert (dc__pim_upsert / dc__pim_upsert_smart or POST /public/pim/items). SPA-baked catalog JSON (public/data/*.json) is never the source of truth; client JSON is a cache/offline mirror only after a store-read proves persisted ids. Prefer waiting longer over baking CSV/charts/media into the zip. Use the Entity Registry (dc__entity_upsert) for parties, farms, animals, equipment instances, and other entity_registry-routed types. Prefer dc__pim_upsert_smart when unsure — the platform routes. Do not treat PIM as a generic dump for every business entity (parties stay in entity_registry). App-scoped GET /public/pim/items (and /cp/pim/products) projects entity_registry operational units already linked to that app as catalog products with the same id — do not remint; duplicate insert of that id is refused. Specs copy registry attributes when present and stay empty otherwise.
- DAM: Use DAM for all files and images (dc__dam_ingest_url or POST /public/dam/assets/upload). Never treat Unsplash, committed zip media, or frontend-only files as the asset source of truth. The app may cache a DAM cdn_url only after ingest proves a persisted asset id. DAM already provides upload, storage, vision extraction, OCR, metadata, thumbnails, and downstream linkage.
- Contextualizer: Use contextualizer-registry read workflows (get_template, resolve_templates, list_templates — the step-template ids ctx-template-get, ctx-template-resolve, ctx-template-list are accepted aliases) and governed MCP write tools (dc__pim_upsert_smart, dc__entity_upsert, dc__propose_template_binding). Template IDs must come from the registry, never invented. On missing templates, the authoring gate returns authoring_proposal_required — promote via dc__confirm_template_authoring before filing records.
- Relationships: Use the Relationship Manager for entity-to-entity connections such as patient-to-profile, meal-to-plan, or asset-to-document.
- Agent rule: App agents should orchestrate platform capabilities, not recreate them.
- Do not: Do not create agents that wrap raw mongodb.search or mongodb.insert when PIM, Entity Registry, DAM, or Contextualizer already fit the use case.
- Do not: Do not build custom vision agents when DAM analyze/process flows already exist.
- Do not: Do not embed fixture data, SPA-baked JSON (public/data/*.json), or committed media as the runtime source of truth; seed the seat DB via governed doors and treat client JSON / DAM cdn_url as cache only.
- Do not: Do not fake chat streaming when /public/agents/chat with stream:true is available.
- Do not: NEVER use MongoClient, mongoose, or any direct MongoDB driver in application code. All data access goes through DC agents with mongodb MCP steps.
- Do not: NEVER use raw ANTHROPIC_API_KEY or OPENAI_API_KEY in application code. All LLM calls go through DC agents with anthropic or openai provider steps.
- Do not: NEVER build standalone Express, Fastify, or Hapi servers that proxy MongoDB or LLM APIs. Frontends call /public/agents/execute for data access.
- Recommended pattern: Data reads: PIM /public/pim/items, Entity Registry /public/entity/entities, DAM /public/dam/assets, or Contextualizer search/aggregate via MCP.
- Recommended pattern: App-scoped data reads/writes: Create app-scoped agents with mongodb MCP steps (search, insert, update, delete). These auto-route to the dedicated DB when configured. Call them via /public/agents/execute from the frontend.
- Recommended pattern: Browser-facing bridge flows: prefer explicit workflows that end with terminal normalized JSON (`workflow_state: "completed"` plus structured `internal_data`) instead of loose multi-turn AI-designed flows.
- Recommended pattern: Image analysis: DAM upload via /public/dam/assets/upload, then DAM process_image or DAM analyze_image plus optional post-processing agent.
- Recommended pattern: Data writes: PIM, Entity Registry, DAM, or Relationships for platform-governed data. Governed records should only be stored once a contextualizer template is resolved via dc__pim_upsert_smart, dc__entity_upsert, or dc__propose_template_binding → dc__confirm_template_binding. On authoring_proposal_required, use dc__confirm_template_authoring before upsert.
- Recommended pattern: Chat: /public/agents/chat with stream:true for conversational SSE streaming with Living Memory auto-extraction.
- Before you build: Your app contract was pre-configured during provisioning. Start with dc__export_app_contract to inspect it. If adjustments are needed, run dc__plan_architecture or dc__scaffold_app_domain to refine. Then validate with dc__validate_app_contract before creating agents or frontend CRUD.

## Data Access Enforcement — MANDATORY

These rules are non-negotiable. They override convenience, speed, and "it works" justifications.

### NEVER do this in app code:
1. fetch() to any third-party API directly from the browser (weather APIs, geocoding, external data services)
   → Use: dc__create_agent with HTTP provider steps, or API Ingest pipelines via /public/api-ingest/pipelines/:id/run

2. Expose API keys via NEXT_PUBLIC_ env vars for external services
   → Use: DevCockpit Vault (dc__store_app_secret) + agent pipeline

3. Use the frontend as source of truth — SPA JSON, localStorage, sessionStorage, baked public/data/*.json, or committed media (images/PDFs/docs in the zip)
   → Use: contextualizer / governed doors into the seat's own database. Products → propose→confirm→PIM (dc__pim_upsert / dc__pim_upsert_smart or POST /public/pim/items). Entities → Entity Registry. Memories → Living Memory. Files → DAM.
   → Exception: UI preferences (theme, layout), offline queues that drain to governed surfaces, session tokens, and cache/offline mirrors ONLY after a store-read proves persisted ids

3b. Treat Unsplash, a committed zip file, or a frontend-only image/PDF path as the digital-asset source of truth
   → Use: dc__dam_ingest_url or POST /public/dam/assets/upload. Cache the DAM cdn_url only after ingest proves a persisted asset id

4. Hardcode template IDs without verifying they exist in the registry
   → Use: dc__discover_app_schema, dc__propose_template_binding, dc__pim_upsert_smart, or contextualizer-registry ctx-template-get / ctx-template-resolve

5. Call copilot/agent workflows that don't exist on the deployed agent
   → Use: dc__list_agents to verify available workflows before coding

### ALWAYS do this:
1. All external API data flows through DevCockpit:
   - API Ingest pipelines for provider data
   - Agent HTTP steps for server-side fetches
   - /public/agents/execute for orchestrated workflows

2. All secrets stored in Vault, never in .env with NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix (except Firebase browser config which is designed to be public)

3. All structured data persisted through governed doors into the seat's own database (that is why each app has a database). The frontend is never the source of truth:
   - Products / compatibility / catalog → PIM (propose→confirm→upsert). Never ship the catalog as SPA-baked JSON as the source of truth.
   - Entities (farms, stations, readings, parties) → Entity Registry
   - Files/images/PDFs → DAM (dc__dam_ingest_url or DAM upload). Never Unsplash-as-SoT or committed zip media only. Cache DAM cdn_url after ingest.
   - Observations/scores/memories → Living Memory
   - Relationships → Relationship Manager
   - Enquire/contact/dealer forms → governed write door + door_log receipt (no fake UI-only submit)
   - Prefer waiting 15–30 minutes longer over baking CSV, charts, or media into the hosted zip

4. Before creating any service file that calls an external API:
   - STOP and check: is there an API Ingest pipeline for this?
   - If yes: use /public/api-ingest/pipelines/:id/run
   - If no: create one via dc__api_ingest_chat first
   - NEVER skip this step because "direct is faster"

### SELF-CHECK before every PR/commit:
- grep -r "fetch(" src/ — is any fetch going to a non-DC URL?
- grep -r "NEXT_PUBLIC_" .env* — is any external API key exposed?
- grep -r "localStorage" src/ — is any app data stored locally as source of truth (not just cache/queue)?
- grep -r "public/data" src/ public/ — is any catalog or app record baked into static JSON as source of truth?
- grep unsplash / public/images / committed media — is a digital asset living only on the frontend instead of DAM?
- grep enquire/contact/dealer form handlers — does every submit persist through a governed door with a door_log receipt?

If the answer to any of these is yes, STOP and refactor through DevCockpit surfaces before committing.

## Platform Laws

- Honest time: dc__emit_event and POST /public/events occurred_at must be ≤ now (+120s skew) or the platform refuses with occurred_at_in_future. Scenario future dates belong in payload attributes, not occurred_at. Browser query is GET /public/events or POST /public/events/query (same door as dc__query_events).
- Event attributes must match the event_types schema; unknown attributes are rejected.
- Machine tokens: entity_type and iku_category are machine-derived tokens (e.g. legal:company, iku-products). Never send display labels (Built-artifact, Specification/Class) as field values.
- Pass-through: caller-provided entity types and relationship attributes are preserved; the model fills blanks only — supply types and attrs explicitly when you know them.
- Identity: structural instances live in the Entity Registry. Ownership is rel:owned_by, never a forced owner field on the record.
- Content documents route to the Entity Registry. rel:member_of spans Organism→Organism living collectives. rel:offspring_of carries parent_role. Organism is for living plants and animals only — do not invent Organism records for products, parties, or catalog rows.
- Binding proposals expire after 30 minutes pending TTL — call dc__list_pending_proposals at session start.
- Frontend is never source of truth: no app may use SPA JSON, localStorage, sessionStorage, baked public/data/*.json, or committed media (images/PDFs/docs in the zip) as the record of what exists. Everything goes through the contextualizer / governed doors into the seat's own database — PIM, Entity Registry, or Living Memory as the plane requires. That is why each app has a database. Prefer waiting 15–30 minutes longer over baking CSV, charts, or media into the hosted zip. Client JSON / localStorage / sessionStorage / a DAM cdn_url may cache or offline-mirror ONLY after a store-read proves persisted ids.
- Seat writes: products, compatibility, and catalog rows MUST live in PIM via propose→confirm→upsert (dc__pim_upsert / dc__pim_upsert_smart or POST /public/pim/items). Digital assets (images, PDFs, docs) MUST go through DAM (dc__dam_ingest_url or DAM upload doors) — never Unsplash-as-SoT or frontend-only files; the app may cache a DAM cdn_url after ingest. Enquire/contact/dealer forms MUST persist through a governed door with a door_log receipt — a UI-only submit that looks successful but writes nothing is a defect. If a client asks to see the data in the database, the seat store must not be empty of what they were shown.

## Schema Governance — Templates

Before writing ANY entity to PIM, Entity Registry, or Living Memory:

1. Resolve the template via governed MCP tools:
   - dc__discover_app_schema — blueprint for your domain
   - dc__propose_template_binding → dc__confirm_template_binding — bind template to your app
   - dc__pim_upsert_smart / dc__entity_upsert — classification + authoring gate (authoring_proposal_required → dc__confirm_template_authoring)
   - contextualizer-registry read workflows: get_template, resolve_templates, list_templates (aliases: ctx-template-get, ctx-template-resolve, ctx-template-list)

2. Use the returned template_id in all writes

3. Pin the template_id as a constant in your code ONLY after step 1 confirms it exists in the registry

4. NEVER invent template IDs. NEVER call contextualizer-pipeline-v5 — it is internal-only and blocked by the MCP gateway.

5. When setting up a new app instance, verify all pinned template IDs still resolve on the new instance's registry.

## Seat Governance — APP SEAT RULEBOOK CORE

This seat is bound by APP SEAT RULEBOOK CORE (served at handshake; repo source `docs/APP_SEAT_RULEBOOK_CORE.md`). Version at last edit: v2.

The full core text arrives in the `handbook` field of the `dc__describe_platform` response — read it at session start. Denials and refusals (403, vault_http_403, scope_denied, permission denied, missing capability), the repair ladder, and escalation are governed by CORE laws 3–5.

Transient errors are not walls: rate limited / 429 → wait and retry once; timeout / 504 → reconnect and retry once. Still failing → treat as a wall under the CORE.

